Hello Hanan, 

yes, this is a known issue with older versions of R. Package namespaces are now needed. While current version of R automatically adds a namespace to the package if it is missing, older versions do not. So ade4 ends up missing one and this causes dependencies problem.

I have added a namespace to ade4 a few days ago but I don't know when we will next release it. In the meantime, updating R should fix your issue. This is anyway to be recommended - R changes fast!

All the best

Thibaut
